    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed and why.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Deterministic household id (`HouseholdKey` + `AssignHouseholdId`)**\n- `HouseholdKey.id(lastName, postcode)` now returns the **first 12 hex chars** of SHA\u2011256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (last name trimmed/whitespace\u2011collapsed/lower\u2011cased; postcode verbatim). Previously it hashed `lastName + address` in full.\n- `AssignHouseholdId` now feeds `postcode` instead of `address`, so owners with the same last name and postcode automatically share the id.\n\n**The `sharesHousehold` request field (`openapi.yml`)**\n- Added a write\u2011only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it binds on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`. Added an `@Mapping(..., ignore = true)` in `OwnerMapper` so it isn't a mapping target on responses.\n\n**The duplicate\u2011household block (new `EnsureUniqueHousehold` + exception/handler)**\n- New `EnsureUniqueHousehold` step (wired after `ensureUniqueIdentity`): if an existing owner shares the request's computed household id and the request did **not** set `sharesHousehold`, it throws the new checked `HouseholdDuplicateException` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateExceptionHandler` \u2192 **409**. Setting `sharesHousehold` bypasses it (declared member). A household needs a postcode, so the block is skipped when none is supplied. Existing owners' ids are recomputed, so matching never depends on a stored value.\n\n**Possible\u2011duplicate flag (`FlagPossibleDuplicate`)**\n- Now keys off the computed `householdId` and explicitly **exempts declared members** (`sharesHousehold` \u21d2 not a suspected duplicate), per spec.\n\n**Household size \u2192 membership level:** `CountHouseholdMembers` already keys off `owner.getHouseholdId()`, so it now automatically uses the new computed id \u2014 no change needed there.\n\n## Verification\n- The provided `AcceptanceTest` (same last name + postcode share the id; different last name differs) passes.\n- I also ran a throwaway test (since removed) confirming the negative paths the spec requires: a second same\u2011household owner **without** `sharesHousehold` returns **409**, and a declared member is created with `possibleDuplicate = false`.\n- Full `mvnw test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green.\n\nOne note: the OpenAPI generator (7.23) treats `writeOnly` as schema-only metadata rather than emitting a Jackson `WRITE_ONLY` access, but the existing serialization omits null fields (the same reason `possibleDuplicateOf` is \"absent when false\"), so `sharesHousehold` does not leak into responses.",
